Package: yourhonor
Title: Calibrate Large Language Model Judges
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jay", "Clark", , "27960665+JsizzleR@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Treat a large language model used as an evaluator (an
    "LLM-as-judge") as a measurement instrument and report its
    psychometric properties. Given a judge and a set of human-labeled
    examples, 'yourhonor' reports chance-corrected agreement between the
    judge and humans (Cohen's kappa, Krippendorff's alpha and Gwet's
    AC1) with bootstrap confidence intervals, the human-human agreement
    ceiling when several raters are supplied, a confusion matrix of where
    they diverge, length-matched paired bias probes (verbosity,
    self-preference and bandwagon, plus position for pairwise judges) and
    chance-corrected test-retest stability across repeated runs. It
    is designed to complement the 'ellmer' and 'vitals' evaluation stack:
    it does not run evaluations, it measures the judge that scores them.
